h schedule(static).\n- Inside each thread's chunk, use #pragma omp simd reduction(+:fx,fy,fz) on j-loop.\n\nAlso ensure that the position update loop is vectorized by adding #pragma omp simd or just rely on compiler. But we can add it.\n\nWe must also include <omp.h> and compile with -fopenmp.\n\nThe Makefile might already have OpenMP flags; but we only change src/nbody.c.\n\nLet's write the new code accordingly.\n\nAlso, note that previous attempts had build failures due to incorrect pragma syntax (e.g., \"simd\" not valid for parallel for). So we must use correct combined or separate directives. The safe approach: outer #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static), and inner #pragma omp simd reduction(+:fx,fy,fz).\n\nWe'll also add a comment about the transformation.\n\nNow, produce JSON output with hypothesis, transformations list (e.g., \"Added restrict qualifiers\", \"Hoisted p[i] coordinates\", \"Applied OpenMP parallel for on outer loop\", \"Applied SIMD reduction on inner loop\"), sources_kept empty array since integration_source_ids is empty, files containing the new src/nbody.c content.\n\nMake sure to escape backslashes in JSON (none here). Use \\n for line breaks."
